'''Italian wedding soup''', known in Italian as '''{{lang|it|minestra maritata}}''',{{efn|Other names include {{lang|it|pignato maritato}} and {{lang|it|pignato grasso}}.<ref name=Bugialli />}} is an [[Italian cuisine|Italian]] [[soup]] consisting of green vegetables and meat in broth. It is central to [[Neapolitan cuisine]], described by food writer Arthur Schwartz as "the king of Neapolitan soups".<ref name=Schwartz1998 /> An Italian-American version of pasta, greens and meatballs in a broth is a staple of Italian restaurants and diners in the United States.<ref name=Schwartz1998 /><ref name=Galarza>{{Cite news |last=Galarza |first=G Daniela |date=January 7, 2021 |title=Hearty and robust, Italian wedding soup is a perfect marriage of meat and vegetables |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/food/2021/01/07/italian-wedding-soup-recipe/ |access-date=April 4, 2026 |work=The Washington Post}}</ref>
